WEBVTT

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.270
Huh? Is it over already?

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.030
You're late, Renge.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.710
We've been waiting here for like a week!

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.050
Sorry about that.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.820
Renge-chan, your mask!

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:18.450
Oops!

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.050
Okay, there we go.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.310
Komadori-san, didn't you say 
you needed to stand by at home?

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.590
My friends are about to risk their 
lives searching for treasure.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.730
I can't sit around at home.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:33.970
Renge-chan...

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.620
Not to mention... We're all friends now.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.070
So I wanted to do something together.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.600
Though I'm not too interested 
in the treasure.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.220
Excuse me.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.430
Are you finished over there?

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:49.170
Oh, sorry about that!

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.610
Please carry on!

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:55.630
Then let us begin this Treasure Club night.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.710
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:11.420
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.050
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.720
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:16.470
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:16.800
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:17.090
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:17.760
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.960
Okay, I want an explanation.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.410
So where do we start?

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:36.010
We will break off in pairs and 
search for the sacred stones.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.940
There are five in total.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.970
<i>There are Zvezda leaders hiding among us.</i>

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.180
<i>I need to identify them first.</i>

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.560
<i>It will be a simple process.</i>

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:57.320
<b>Visualization</b>

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.810
<i>We take a UDO reading of every pair,</i>

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.320
<i>then we have the pairs with 
high readings split up,</i>

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.980
<i>form new pairs, and take 
their readings again.</i>

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.790
<i>If we repeat this process a few times,</i>

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.780
<i>we should have a short list of candidates.</i>

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:08.290
<i>Then I capture all of them inside my barrier.</i>

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.230
The stones are meant to be 
placed inside the Udo Bride,

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.290
and they're about this big.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:21.420
Do these stones have a 
white udo marking on them?

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:21.930
Huh?

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.580
Known as badabing badaboom,

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.130
they were the second most sacred object to

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.470
the Ancient Udogawa, after Udo.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.770
I was about to go into that.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.070
That's right. She's absolutely correct.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:42.390
So we're supposed to look for those stones?

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:43.200
Yes.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:44.980
Okay!

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.200
Boys, let's go find us some treasure!

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.290
Yeah!

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.890
Madame, what is a badabing badaboom?

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.700
Are you asking me to answer that question?

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:58.500
Forgive me!

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:01.970
All of this is nothing more 
than an act to achieve our mission.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:07.300
We made up the treasure, 
so why would badabings exist?

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:09.310
<i>What was that?!</i>

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.920
I was expecting some 
strange people to show up.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.110
The mission to capture Zvezda 
continues regardless.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.020
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.280
<i>It's a trap...</i>

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.110
<i>They must be White Light.</i>

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.740
<i>Why didn't I notice this sooner?</i>

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.740
<i>I must warn the others at once!</i>

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:33.780
Here it is!

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:36.730
An emergency transmission from General Pepel!

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:37.580
Let's see...

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.400
Ha-me-ha-me-ha.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.110
What's that mean?!

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:46.470
It's a trap

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.940
The chief is supposed to be 
disguised as Nitobe Inazo.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.590
Not King Kamehameha.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.180
I know that.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.620
Oh, there's more.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:52.670
Let's see...

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:58.110
They-be-long-to-twi-light?

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.230
What's that mean? I don't get it.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:06.110
They belong to White Light.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:05.180
Is it a lyric from one of 
those ballads he likes so much?

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.330
Go ask him!

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:08.120
Got it!

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.670
For some reason, I have a 
bad feeling about this...

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:22.170
This is more like a test of 
courage than a treasure hunt.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.270
I don't like walking 
through school at night...

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:27.840
Mind if I ask why?

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:32.060
Nobody else is supposed to be around, 
but it feels like I'm being watched.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.520
I had a feeling this might happen...

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.320
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey, hey, hey!

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.340
Renge! Follow me!

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:49.570
You're a completely different 
person at night, Kate-chan.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:52.210
I found something! I found something!

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:53.940
Really? Let me see.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:04.050
In this situation, it's a good idea to sing.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:05.800
Y-You're right.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.970
Treasure! Treasure—

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.550
Sorry, it's just my phone.

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:15.060
Uh-oh...

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:16.320
What's wrong?

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.170
It's someone from work.

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:19.380
Excuse me for a moment.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.240
This is White Robin.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.400
What's wrong, Egret? Is there an emergency?

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.520
Where are you right now?

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:30.910
Huh? Where am I?

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.570
A-At home.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.210
You're lying.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:38.030
Wh-What? Why would you say that?

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:41.860
Can you please not disappoint me again?

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.370
Um, I can explain.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.990
I don't want to hear any excuses.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.100
Your mission was to stand by at home.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.660
Return to your assigned position.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:51.300
Okay...

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.690
Renge, look at this!

00:06:57.690 --> 00:06:58.980
Roboko found one!

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.230
Huh? What's wrong?

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.270
Oh, well, actually...

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.890
Wow, it's true!

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:08.330
There's an udo on it!

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:10.700
Is something the matter?

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:13.700
Look at this, Madame!

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:19.000
Let's have a look then.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.910
What was that for?!

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:32.390
There are many fake sacred stones.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.930
This is an ancient method of appraisal.

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:38.180
If the stone chips or cracks 
even a little, it's fake.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:41.390
There's a better way to test the stones.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.690
Throw the stones in the pool?

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:46.930
That's right.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:51.110
If these are real, there should 
be some kind of reaction.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:15.750
It appears that they were fake.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.260
That can't be right!

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.930
Why don't you ask the girl next to you, then?

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:21.520
Well?!

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:29.000
It appears that the leading Ancient 
Udogawa authority has nothing to say.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:30.530
What's so funny?!

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:33.070
All of this is funny.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:36.660
Especially the fact that you were 
stupid enough to think you could

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.490
find treasure so easily!

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:43.080
Uh, I don't think you 
need to be that shocked...

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:44.680
Right!

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:47.490
Kate-chan's working hard to find treasure!

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.210
You shouldn't talk to her like that!

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:52.450
Working hard to find treasure?

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:53.590
Y-Yes...

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:57.020
Very well.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:00.930
If you believe in them, you can stay here.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:11.980
Perhaps the Udogawa dance will help.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:13.280
That's it!

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.180
Dance!

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:14.950
I can't.

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:18.540
The emptiness I feel after 
doing that is unbearable.

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:19.620
I can't.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:22.040
Just start dancing!

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:33.890
The UDO scanners have confirmed that 
the members here are all clean.

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:35.380
Let them go.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.010
Tell them to leave school immediately.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:37.730
Yes.

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:41.470
What about the readings on 
the members by the pool?

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.460
They're high.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:43.850
As I suspected.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.170
That just leaves the question of how 
we separate her from our enemies.

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:53.430
Asuta-kun, do the treasure exercise!

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:54.980
You, too, Komadori-san?

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:57.880
I'm still mad about how she made fun of us!

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.420
Exactly, Renge!

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:00.800
Now, dance, Asuta!

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:01.870
I can't...

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:12.920
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:16.810
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:20.930
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:25.040
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:29.270
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:29.270
Give me a break...

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:33.110
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:36.490
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:40.460
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:44.120
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:47.710
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:51.580
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:55.360
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:59.320
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:02.800
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:06.360
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:12.530
Treasure! Treasure! Treasure! Hey!

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:08.770
I know it will come...

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:15.110
What's this?!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.180
Transmission from Obs.

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:19.440
UDO readings are spiking.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.030
Impossible!

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:24.420
UDO levels are continuing to rise.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:25.240
These readings are...

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:27.970
Change in plans.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.750
Begin the operation now.

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:32.540
Something's coming.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:33.930
Roboko?

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:36.460
It's me.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.890
The Treasure Club is run by White Light.

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:40.800
Madame M is probably...

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:50.560
What is this?!

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:51.730
A barrier.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:52.310
Huh?

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:53.830
How?

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:54.610
Huh?

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:56.270
Why?

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:57.710
Renge-chan?

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:00.950
Oh, sorry. I just remembered that 
there's something I need to do!

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:01.530
Bye!

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:02.570
Komadori-san?

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:05.080
What are you doing?!

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.680
Fool! What do you think
you're doing at a time like this?

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:08.490
Look over there!

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:14.870
My instincts were right!

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:16.920
This is proof that the treasure exists!

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:25.090
Yes?

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:28.170
Egret, where are you right now?

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:30.310
Are you in the middle of an operation?

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:38.530
Huh?

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.440
Hello? Egret?

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.140
What happened?

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:47.450
What?

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.140
It can't be.

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:53.010
Why are they here?

00:12:56.750 --> 00:13:00.010
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:00.000
<b>Episode 7             After School Treasure Club (Part 2)</b>

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:04.010
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:04.000
<b>Episode 7             After School Treasure Club (Part 2)</b>

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:15.890
What is this...

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:26.930
Treasure!

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:29.200
Huh?

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:44.510
Huh?

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:47.970
Wh-What?

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:55.020
What's that?!

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.700
The treasure is over there!

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:30.180
What is this place?

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.930
It looks like our school, right?

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:38.120
Huh? Where'd she go?

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:41.670
I found you! Give me the treasure!

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:44.370
What? That's it?

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:48.450
Oh. No, I'm not complaining.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.200
Who's she talking to?

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:53.620
Come on, you must be joking.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.120
Wait, seriously?!

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:56.590
Is she over there?

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:02.730
But I'm not prepared yet!

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.110
Hold on! Stop right there!

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:07.140
I said to stop!

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:13.180
Hey...

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:38.980
It stopped?

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:41.820
Why?

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:42.710
Kate?!

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:50.050
Why won't you let me conquer you?

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:01.600
Asuta...

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:05.230
No! I'm Dva!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.710
A member of Zvezda!

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:08.360
One of your adorable henchmen!

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:14.980
Asuta!

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:18.240
Didn't you hear me?!

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.430
I said I'm Dva!

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:23.430
Asuta!

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:28.480
What are you afraid of, Asuta?

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:30.270
Shouldn't that be obvious?!

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:37.820
That was...

00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:44.730
What is the meaning of this?

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:46.500
Why are they here?

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:49.730
Didn't you say that I would be 
in charge of this operation?

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:53.500
UDO readings have exceeded acceptable levels,

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:57.160
so the operation is no 
longer in our jurisdiction.

00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:01.680
The operation against Zvezda 
has moved to the next phase.

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:05.780
The operation is off.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:07.980
Retreat immediately.

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:08.860
But...

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:16.680
Plamya!

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:19.760
Too much smoke, damn it.

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:24.890
This strange smoke has disabled Roboko.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.310
We must retreat for now!

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:28.080
Fool!

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:33.130
If we don't defend this position, 
Kate and Asuta can't return!

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:43.090
I can't accept the methods they're using!

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:48.610
Huh?

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:50.830
Who are they fighting?

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.640
Dva-san?

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:02.660
Wait!

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:05.330
I said to wait!

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:27.080
Oh, boy...

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:34.960
When the chosen one and udo finally meet,

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.980
the world will again be conquered.

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:42.160
By a child that takes the 
appearance of a devil.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:07.870
I was born to conquer this world.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:14.320
However, the same could be said of anyone.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:19.840
Every person has the potential 
to conquer the world!

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:26.680
If you refuse to let me conquer you,

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:31.920
you should try to conquer me!

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:37.610
Your actions and words never match!

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:44.930
Conquest

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:48.500
time!

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:45.100
<i>After that, life did not return to normal.</i>

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:51.020
School 
is 
closed

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:51.020
<i>The sanctuary I vowed to 
protect was quickly conquered,</i>

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:55.000
<i>leaving me with nowhere else to go.</i>

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:19.650
<i>But for some reason, 
I was fine with that fact.</i>

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:23.640
So, what happened to the treasure?

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.690
Stop mumbling.

00:21:27.690 --> 00:21:28.600
What happened?

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:31.320
Well...

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:34.310
You don't remember?!

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.710
I didn't forget everything.

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:39.030
I remember what happened up 
to when we jumped in the pool.

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:40.570
So you forgot the important part!

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.380
Man...

00:21:43.310 --> 00:21:44.930
What was that all about?

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:46.480
But...

00:21:48.170 --> 00:21:51.240
But somehow, I...

00:21:54.610 --> 00:21:55.930
There you are.

00:21:55.930 --> 00:21:56.890
What is it?

00:21:57.930 --> 00:22:03.710
We've identified the men who 
appeared during that treasure mishap.

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:06.760
It was the Tokyo Military Special Force

00:22:07.850 --> 00:22:10.430
under the command of the Tokyo governor.

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:20.570
We are always ready to provide support.

00:22:22.010 --> 00:22:26.680
Of course. That is why we exist.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.460
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:24:01.050 --> 00:24:04.790
The rain has to stop, 
just like the sun has to set.

00:24:05.140 --> 00:24:09.140
At some point, you get sick 
of unlimited cake buffets.

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:12.470
Moderation is important when having fun.

00:24:12.470 --> 00:24:15.370
I hope I get to go to school again.

00:24:15.370 --> 00:24:18.840
I feel that Renge-chan and 
I are good friends now.

00:24:18.840 --> 00:24:21.580
Yes, friends are wonderful.

00:24:21.580 --> 00:24:24.020
They are the best thing in life.

00:24:24.020 --> 00:24:26.210
Don't you have any friends, Yasu-kun?

00:24:26.210 --> 00:24:28.570
Come on! Of course I do!

00:24:27.020 --> 00:24:31.160
<b>Episode 8                   The Falcon Has Landed</b>
